  "id": "employment-psychology",
  "term": "employment psychology",
  "definition": "Employment psychology refers to the feelings, attitudes, and mental tendencies people have about getting a job, such as confusion, anxiety, pessimism, or a preference for stable work. In this study context, it describes how university students’ views of the job market shape their employment choices and intentions.",
